---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Navbar from '../components/nav/Navbar.astro';
import Footer from '../components/ui/Footer.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Documentation — Starmesh"
  description="Starmesh documentation: getting started, asking in Claude or ChatGPT, connecting your CRM and calls, and support."
>
  <Navbar />
  <main class="doc-page">
    <h1>Documentation</h1>

    <section>
      <h2>What is Starmesh?</h2>
      <p>Starmesh reads your CRM and your customer calls, and answers two questions: which deals are real, and how an account is doing. You ask in Claude or ChatGPT (beta). Every answer cites the call or the record it came from.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Getting started</h2>
      <ol>
        <li>Go to <a href="https://app.starmesh.ai">app.starmesh.ai</a> and sign up with Google or email.</li>
        <li>You land on a sample sales book (a fictional company). Look around, then ask questions about it in Claude or ChatGPT.</li>
        <li>To use your own data, connect your CRM and call recorder on the Connect page and choose a plan. <a href="/contact">Contact us</a> to agree the plan.</li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Ask in Claude or ChatGPT</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Claude:</strong> install the <a href="https://github.com/starmesh-ai/starmesh-claude-plugin#install" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Starmesh plugin</a>, or open the Ask button in the app.</li>
        <li><strong>ChatGPT (beta):</strong> add Starmesh as a custom connector. This needs a ChatGPT plan with developer mode (Plus, Pro, Business or Enterprise). The app shows the exact steps and link.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>What you can ask</h2>
      <table class="doc-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Question</th><th>What you get</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Which deals look shaky?</td><td>Open pipeline by stage, and the deals the calls do not support: no next step, an open objection, a long silence</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Is this deal moving?</td><td>Open commitments, unresolved objections, days since last contact, who is engaged, and whether the last two calls got better or worse, with quotes. A deal with too little to read is called a thin read</td></tr>
          <tr><td>How is this account doing?</td><td>What happened, what changed and what is still open, in order, tied to the call each moment came from</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Who is doing the talking?</td><td>Rep talk share and questions per call, next to the team median</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <p class="doc-note">Coverage against quota is not shown until quota data is connected.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Connecting your data</h2>
      <p>Use the Connect page in the app. Connect your CRM and call recorder first. Email and calendar are optional.</p>
      <table class="doc-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Type</th><th>Sources</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>CRM</td><td>Salesforce, Attio</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Calls</td><td>Zoom, Microsoft Teams, Google Meet, Gong, Granola</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Email</td><td>Gmail</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Calendar</td><td>Google Calendar</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <p>Starmesh matches each call to the right deal and account. You can review and correct those matches under Review links in the app. On a team, an Admin can make some sources required for everyone.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Plans</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Sample data:</strong> free, no time limit.</li>
        <li><strong>Your own CRM and calls:</strong> paid, set up with us. How far back Starmesh reads and how often it syncs depend on the plan.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Security and access</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Sources connect with OAuth. You can disconnect any of them.</li>
        <li>Encryption at rest and in transit.</li>
        <li>Each person's calls, email and calendar stay their own, even on a team plan.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Disconnecting a source or deleting data</h2>
      <p>To disconnect a source, open Settings in the app, go to Data sources and disconnect it.</p>
      <p>To remove everything, open Settings, then Account. Reset removes every connected source and the data synced from it and keeps your sign-in. Delete removes your account and everything connected to it.</p>
      <p>You can also email <a href="mailto:support@starmesh.ai">support@starmesh.ai</a>.</p>

      <h3>Removing Starmesh from your Zoom Apps</h3>
      <ol>
        <li>Log in to your Zoom account and navigate to the Zoom App Marketplace.</li>
        <li>Click Manage >> Added Apps or search for the "Starmesh" app.</li>
        <li>Select the "Starmesh" app.</li>
        <li>Click Remove.</li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Need help?</h2>
      <p>Email: <a href="mailto:support@starmesh.ai">support@starmesh.ai</a></p>
    </section>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .doc-page {
    max-width: 900px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 6rem 1.5rem 4rem;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1.75rem;
  }

  .doc-page h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 2.5rem);
    font-weight: 800;
    margin-bottom: 0.25rem;
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, #6366F1, #8B5CF6, #A855F7);
    -webkit-background-clip: text;
    -webkit-text-fill-color: transparent;
    background-clip: text;
  }

  .doc-page h2 {
    font-size: 1.375rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: #FAFAFA;
    margin-top: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    padding-bottom: 0.375rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.06);
  }

  .doc-page h3 {
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: #FAFAFA;
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .doc-page p,
  .doc-page ul,
  .doc-page ol {
    font-size: 1rem;
    color: #A1A1AA;
    line-height: 1.65;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }

  .doc-page ul,
  .doc-page ol {
    padding-left: 1.5rem;
  }

  .doc-page li {
    margin-bottom: 0.4rem;
  }

  .doc-page a {
    color: #818CF8;
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 500;
    transition: color 0.2s ease;
  }

  .doc-page a:hover {
    color: #A855F7;
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  .doc-table {
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    margin: 1rem 0 1.5rem 0;
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    background: #111114;
    border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.07);
    border-radius: 12px;
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .doc-table th,
  .doc-table td {
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.06);
    padding: 0.75rem 1rem;
    text-align: left;
    color: #A1A1AA;
  }

  .doc-table tr:last-child td {
    border-bottom: none;
  }

  .doc-table th {
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.03);
    color: #FAFAFA;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 0.875rem;
  }

  .doc-table tr:hover td {
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.02);
  }

  .doc-note {
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    color: #71717A;
    padding: 0.75rem 1rem;
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.03);
    border-left: 3px solid rgba(129, 140, 248, 0.7);
    border-radius: 0 8px 8px 0;
    margin: 1rem 0;
  }

  .doc-page section {
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .doc-page {
      padding: 5rem 1rem 3rem;
    }

    .doc-table th,
    .doc-table td {
      padding: 0.5rem 0.75rem;
      font-size: 0.875rem;
    }
  }
</style> 